# Copy to .dev.vars (git-ignored) for local development.
#
# ENVIRONMENT=development makes the magic link print to the wrangler console
# instead of being emailed, so the app works without an email provider.
ENVIRONMENT=development
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:5173
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=a-long-random-string-just-for-local-dev
EMAIL_FROM=Sparmin <hello@sparmin.scottlovegrove.co.uk>

# Leave unset to print magic links to the console. Set it to send real mail.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...

# Web Push. Leave unset and the app simply has no push: /api/push/config reports
# no key and the notifications card says so, rather than offering a toggle that
# cannot work. A shared development pair is in .dev.vars.sops — see the README —
# or generate your own; the production keys are Cloudflare secrets, set with
# `npm run secret`, and are not in this repo.
#
# The third value push needs, VAPID_SUBJECT, is a plain `vars` entry in
# wrangler.jsonc rather than a secret, and wrangler binds those alongside this
# file — so it is already set in development and only belongs here if you want to
# override it. All three must be present or the Worker treats push as
# unconfigured.
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=B...
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=...
